// PILOT NOTE: the sheet's own variant for this spell is `Transform`, and this is the first
// attempt anywhere in the compendium to author a player spell with it. After reading
// `common/src/comp/ability.rs` (the `Transform` variant), `common/src/states/transform.rs`, and
// `server/src/events/entity_manipulation.rs::transform_entity`, `Transform` was found unusable
// for this spell and is NOT used here. Concretely, `Transform`:
//   1. Replaces the target's entire body/stats/inventory/skillset with a brand-new `EntityConfig`
//      loaded from a `target: String` asset path (`transform.rs`'s `StaticData::target`) -- it
//      is a full entity swap, not a stat-modifying buff, so a player's real gear/stats would be
//      discarded, not preserved "along with all it wears and carries" as the sheet requires.
//   2. Sets the transformed entity's `Presence` to `PresenceKind::Possessor` and explicitly
//      disables persistence for it (`transform_entity`'s "Disable persistence" block) -- there
//      is no code path anywhere in this engine that reverts `Possessor` back to
//      `PresenceKind::Character` or restores the pre-transform body. Every existing `Transform`
//      RON (`cursekeeper/transform.ron`, `debug/evolve.ron`, `debug/eaglify.ron`) is a one-way,
//      permanent-until-a-human-intervenes admin/debug/lore gimmick, not a timed effect.
//   3. Has no `duration` field at all -- `buildup_duration`/`recover_duration` only cover the
//      cast animation, not how long the new form lasts.
// None of this matches a Concentration(60)-duration, willing-target, fully reversible buff that
// "collapses" under a condition. Using `Transform` as-shipped for `gaseous_form` would
// permanently strip the target's real character and never give it back -- shipping that as a
// player spell would be a serious, silent regression, not a faithful rendering of the sheet.
//
// Ships instead as the established touch-ally pattern (spider_climb.ron/weave_transfusion.ron
// in this folder: SelfBuff can only ever land on the caster, and the sheet's own range: Touch +
// "a willing creature you touch" third-person phrasing calls for the ally-touch shape).
// "Dissolves into vapor, seeps through gaps, floats" is modeled with ProtectingWard
// (partial damage resistance -- gaseous form's real defensive core in the source material) as
// the nearest existing primitive; the "seep through narrow gaps" and "collapses near death"
// riders have no engine hook and are dropped, not silently reinterpreted.
//
// Reconciliation note for whoever authors the next `Transform`-variant spell: this pilot's
// conclusion is that `Transform`, in its current shape, has no viable use as a *timed, willing,
// reversible* player spell effect at all -- only as a one-way permanent transformation (which no
// sheet spell in this school calls for). A real fix would need new Rust: storing the
// pre-transform body/stats and a timer-driven revert event. Until that exists, any other
// Transform-labeled sheet spell should default to the same substitution approach used here
// rather than re-attempting the literal variant.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 55.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Buff((
                kind: ProtectingWard,
                dur_secs: 60.0,
                strength: Value(0.5),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Transmutation), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(30.0)),
)
